2. Option 1 sahi hai kyunki jab do identical periodic waves same line ke along opposite directions mein travel karti hain, toh unka linear superposition ek **Standing (Stationary) Wave** form karta hai:
   - **Nodes (निस्पंद)**: Medium mein wo points jahan destructive interference complete hota hai, resulting in **permanently zero displacement amplitude** (aur maximum pressure/strain variation);
   - **Antinodes (प्रस्पंद)**: Wo points jahan constructive interference maximized hota hai, resulting in **maximum displacement amplitude** (aur minimum pressure/strain variation);
   - **Spatial Separation**: Kisi bhi **do consecutive nodes (ya do consecutive antinodes) ke beech ki distance strictly $\mathbf{\frac{\lambda}{2}}$** (half wavelength) hoti hai, jabki ek adjacent node aur antinode ke beech ki distance $\frac{\lambda}{4}$ hoti hai.
3. Option 2 aur Option 3 galat spatial node separations state karte hain.

